# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

### Added

- **Encode is transport-neutral (`encode.Options.Events`)**: the encode batch
  now narrates through the shared event system — a start stage, one config
  info line, one `item_done` per file (failures carry the error), a terminal
  `summary` carrying the ok/failed/skipped tallies, and the dry-run command
  echo — emitted as structured `event.Event`s on an `event.Sink` with nothing
  written to the terminal when one is supplied. The CLI passes no sink, so
  `provenance encode` output is byte-for-byte unchanged; a TUI or worker
  transport can now consume encode progress like every other operation.
- **Run history on the CLI (`provenance history`)**: every run that goes
  through `app.Download` — CLI `grab`, `watch run` (including `--every`
  repeats) and `collect sync` — now records one history entry (URLs,
  ok/fail/skip counts, duration, total bytes, error text; dry runs are not
  recorded). New command: `provenance history` (bare = list), with `list`,
  `show <ID>` (full or unique prefix; prints title, duration, counts,
  output dir, error, URLs, per-file results when recorded), `delete <ID>`,
  and `clear --yes`. Stored under the user cache dir, like the TUI's history.
- **`provenance watch run --every <interval>`**: run a watch (or all watches)
  on a repeating interval (Go duration: `30m`, `24h`, `7d`…). The first run
  starts immediately; per-run errors are reported without stopping the loop;
  Ctrl-C cancels the in-flight run and exits cleanly. Each completed tick
  records a history entry and updates the watch's last-run time.
- **`provenance doctor`**: read-only prerequisite check for yt-dlp, ffmpeg,
  ffprobe, Chrome, an optional cookies file, the cache directory, and the
  archive database (`PROVENANCE_DATABASE_URL`, pinged with a short timeout and
  reported by host only). Exit code is non-zero when a required check fails;
  the command never triggers tool auto-install.
- **Deterministic vault revision IDs**: `computeRevisionID` now excludes the
  wall-clock capture time, so re-ingesting the same capture manifest produces
  the same content-addressed revision ID and retries/resumes are idempotent
  instead of accumulating duplicate revisions.
- **Vault invariants under test**: new test coverage for ingest (path
  traversal rejection, hash-mismatch abort with no blobs stored, missing-file
  skip, content dedupe, revision round-trip), revision diffing, retention
  pruning (newest-N per collection, other collections untouched), and
  garbage collection (referenced blobs always survive, dry-run deletes
  nothing).
- **Transport-neutral extractor paths (Phase 1)**: every path reachable from
  `engine.Resolve` and `engine.Download` — Instagram, X/Twitter, hashtag search,
  Reddit, Album, the browser fallback, and the dispatcher batch/pool paths — now
  emits structured events instead of writing to a terminal, and writes nothing to
  stdout/stderr when the operation carries an event sink. Stable machine-readable
  reason codes are defined in `internal/event/reasons.go`; legacy CLI narration is
  preserved byte-for-byte when no sink is supplied, so CLI golden output is
  unchanged.
- **Event sink on the operation context** (`internal/event.WithSink` /
  `SinkFrom`): nested helper functions emit through the context instead of
  threading a sink through every signature. `event.Emit` resolves the context sink
  when no explicit sink is passed. New `event.KindInfo` carries operation facts
  (pagination decisions, fallbacks taken) that are neither warnings nor terminal
  item outcomes; `internal/render` renders it.
- **Event redaction** (`internal/redact`): `Detail` bounds, normalizes, and removes
  cookie/authorization/bearer/token/session fragments, and `URL` drops query
  strings and fragments, so events never carry raw platform response bodies,
  cookies, auth headers, or secret-bearing URLs. Response-body, error, and
  fallback narration now emits stable facts (for example a status code) instead
  of body previews or raw error text.
- **Operation-scoped workspace** (`internal/workspace`): `Download` runs in a
  workspace that records what already existed and reports only files the operation
  created, excluding engine bookkeeping directories and in-progress partials.
  `engine.Config.IsolatedWorkspace` gives each operation its own subdirectory, the
  only arrangement that separates two concurrent jobs sharing a parent directory.
- **Typed capability probe** (`internal/capability`, `engine.Capabilities`,
  `engine.ToolStatus`): reports yt-dlp (required), ffmpeg, ffprobe, and Chrome
  without installing a tool, downloading anything, or mutating the filesystem, so
  a health check has no side effects. `engine.Config.AutoInstall` is false by
  default; the CLI keeps its historical auto-install behavior.
- **Engine-owned dependencies** (`internal/extractor.Deps`): the X/Twitter query-ID
  cache and the tool paths are now per-engine instead of process-global. The
  transport stays a package-level immutable, concurrency-safe shared service.
- **Cancellable retry/backoff paths**: `sleepCtx` replaces `time.Sleep` in every
  extractor retry and rate-limit backoff (Instagram, X/Twitter, hashtag search,
  Reddit, Album) and in the downloader's speed-limit wait, so a canceled
  operation stops instead of waiting out a backoff. Server-supplied
  `Retry-After` values are parsed by one shared helper (`retryAfterDelay`) and
  capped at 5 minutes; an over-cap value emits a `retry_after_capped` warning
  event.
- **Backoff and event-fact invariants under test**: fixture-server tests prove
  each native extractor's rate-limit and 5xx backoff honors cancellation, an
  over-cap `Retry-After` is clipped with a warning, error-response events carry
  only stable status facts (canary response bodies never leak into events or
  errors), and a speed-limited download aborts promptly on cancellation.
- **Bounded sink close**: `event.Notifier.Close` waits at most a grace period for
  an in-flight delivery, so a blocked foreign sink can never stall the caller.
- **Single X post resolution**: `https://x.com/<user>/status/<id>` is now a
  distinct source kind (`TwSourceStatus`) resolved through the
  `TweetResultByRestId` operation, so a status URL fetches exactly the post it
  names instead of paginating the author's whole timeline. Trailing media-index
  segments (`/video/1`, `/photo/1`) are ignored, the post id must be numeric, and
  `ScanTwitterResolved` reports `resolve.KindSingle` for these sources. The query
  id has no hard-coded fallback (discovered from the web-client JS or
  `TWITTER_QUERY_TWEET_RESULT_BY_REST_ID`).
- **`encode --remove-original`**: deletes each source file only after its encode
  succeeds. A failed encode leaves its source in place, and `--dry-run` never
  removes anything.
- **Context-cancellable importers**: `ImportGit`, `ImportPDF`, `ImportDocs`,
  `ImportOpenAPI`, and `ImportWeb` now take the operation context. The CLI
  passes the signal context and the TUI its root context, so Ctrl-C stops an
  import. Git subprocesses run in their own process group and the whole group
  is killed on cancellation (Unix), with a bounded `WaitDelay` on every
  platform; the docs crawl uses context-aware HTTP requests; the web importer's
  chromedp allocator inherits the caller context instead of
  `context.Background()`; capture-failure narration is emitted as a structured
  `web_scrape_failed` warning (legacy CLI text unchanged without a sink).
- **Importers under test**: first test coverage for `internal/importers` —
  git-arg validation (ext:: transport, scheme allowlist, dash-prefixed refs),
  mid-clone and mid-crawl cancellation against fixture servers, PDF/OpenAPI
  ingest into a temp vault with blob verification, docs scope/maxPages bounds,
  web pre-flight validation, UTF-8-safe truncation, and the narration
  transport-neutrality contract. No test contacts a live service.
- **Config, citation, and resolve under test**: the persisted `config.Config`
  JSON shape (field names, omitempty behavior, round trip) and the
  capture-options mapping are pinned; `internal/citation` gains round-trip,
  formatter, and entity-mapping coverage; `internal/resolve` pins the
  `scan --json` field-name contract and error-category semantics. Every
  package in the module now has tests.
- **SSRF dial guard on the shared extractor transport**: the private-network
  dial control from `downloader.New` is exported as `downloader.NewDialer` and
  now also protects the extractors' shared transport, so platform-supplied URLs
  (for example album CDN hosts) cannot reach loopback, RFC1918, link-local, or
  cloud-metadata addresses even via a non-literal hostname. Downloader resume,
  416 recovery, redirect, and dial-guard behavior are covered by new hermetic
  tests.

### Changed

- **`encode`: output now lands in the source directory by default** (in place)
  instead of a `<dir>/av1_qN` subdirectory, and no per-file log files are
  written; ffmpeg stderr is discarded. `--out` still redirects. The scan skips
  its own in-place `<base>.<suffix>.mkv` outputs so re-runs do not re-encode
  them, while a user's own `.mkv` files are still collected.
- **`encode`: `--devices` is auto-detected when unset** — QSV pins the Intel render
  nodes (PCI vendor `8086`) and AMF the AMD nodes (`1002`/`1022`) found in
  `/dev/dri` via `/sys/class/drm`, sorted by node number; NVENC uses GPU index
  0. The previous hard-coded `/dev/dri/renderD128` default is gone — a box
  whose lowest-numbered node is a non-Intel GPU (for example an RTX 3090
  without AV1 hardware encode) no longer defaults to a node that cannot
  encode. If no node matches the vendor, every node is pinned so the failure
  is loud; with no render nodes at all nothing is pinned and the encoder
  library chooses.
- `dispatcher.PrintSummary` is now a presentation adapter taking an `io.Writer`;
  reusable paths emit `EventSummary` and never write to a terminal themselves.
- The TUI no longer reassigns `os.Stdout`/`os.Stderr`. It consumes events through
  an `event.Sink` (`internal/tui.teaSink`), which is safe to run alongside other
  consumers in a shared process.
- `Notifier.Close` is bounded by a grace period rather than waiting indefinitely
  for a slow sink.
- **Rate-limit waits are bounded**: a server `Retry-After` longer than 5 minutes
  is clipped to the cap with a one-line notice, so a hostile or broken platform
  response cannot stall a run for hours. Waits within the cap are unchanged.
- **`archive import-docs` validates the URL scheme**: only `http`/`https` seeds
  are accepted, matching `import-web`. Other schemes previously produced an
  empty revision instead of a clear error.

### Fixed

- **Invalid `--min-size`/`--max-size` values are rejected**: `manifest.ParseSize`
  silently converted `NaN`, `Inf`, negative values, and sizes that overflow
  int64 into wrapped/negative byte counts, producing nonsensical filters. These
  now return a clear error instead.
- **Extractor routing uses exact domains, not substrings**: `dispatcher.Classify`
  and the platform URL parsers matched hosts with `strings.Contains`, so
  lookalikes (`instagram.com.evil.net`, `notx.com`, `x.com.evil.net`,
  `bunkr.cr.evil.net`) were routed to native extractors. Those extractors then
  resolved a *different real resource* than the URL named instead of letting
  yt-dlp handle the actual host. Routing and `ParseIgURL`/`ParseTwSource`/
  `ParseRdURL`/album host tables now require the exact domain or a subdomain
  (ports and trailing dots normalized).
- **Instagram shortcode overflow**: `igShortcodeToID` silently overflowed
  int64 for codes longer than 11 characters (and had a nonsensical >28-char
  truncation that decoded the wrong prefix). Overlong/invalid codes now return
  0, so the caller falls back to the server-rendered post page instead of
  requesting an unrelated post id.
- **Citation references round-trip**: `citation.Parse` split at the last `@`,
  so entity ids containing `@` (for example `medium.com/@user/...` URLs) failed
  to parse. It now splits at the first `@` and first `#`, rejects empty
  components, and round-trips `Format` for URL-shaped entity ids.
- **Watch runs recover crashed "running" status**: a run killed mid-flight left
  `last_run_status: running` forever. `watch run` now records such a run as
  `interrupted` (preserving its start time and partial duration) before
  starting the next one, so status history stays honest. Covered by store
  tests for recovery, idempotency, and completed-run preservation.
- **Session transitions survive concurrent modification**: when a save hit a
  version conflict, the reload replaced the in-memory entries and the retry
  saved the unmodified state — silently dropping the status transition (a
  failed URL could stay "running" forever). The retry now re-applies the
  pending transition after reloading, matching `ResetRunning`'s behavior.
  Covered by a conflict-injection regression test.
- **Blob store is safe under concurrent Puts**: parallel stores of identical
  content shared one deterministic `.tmp` path, and the loser deleted the
  winner's in-progress file — potentially renaming a partially written blob
  into place under the wrong hash. Each attempt now uses a unique temp file,
  re-hashes the content while copying (so a source mutated mid-put can never
  be stored under a stale address), and `List` ignores temp/stray entries so
  garbage collection cannot delete an in-progress write. Covered by a
  concurrent-put race test and a List-filtering test.
- **`encode --remove-original` verifies the output first**: an ffmpeg exit 0
  with a missing or empty output file is now reported as a failed encode, so
  the source is never deleted on a phantom success. Successful-encode tests
  now exercise a faithful fake that writes the output file.
- **Downloader resume edge cases**: a zero-byte `.part` left by an interrupted
  attempt no longer blocks every future download of the destination (`O_EXCL`
  became `O_TRUNC` for fresh starts). A 416 "range not satisfiable" response no
  longer deletes a `.part` that may already hold the complete file: when the
  server's `Content-Range` total matches the `.part` size it is renamed into
  place, and without confirmation the `.part` is preserved instead of
  destroyed. The already-downloaded skip and 416 completion paths now report
  `LastPath`/`LastHash` like a normal download and clean up stale `.part` files.
- **Canceled git imports no longer hang or orphan helpers**: `git clone` spawns
  remote helpers (for example `git-remote-https`) that inherit the output pipes.
  Killing only the parent left them holding the pipes open, so `CombinedOutput`
  waited for EOF forever and the helpers kept running. The clone now runs in its
  own process group, cancellation kills the whole group, and a bounded
  `WaitDelay` guarantees the import returns even if a pipe lingers.
- **Auto-install no longer panics**: `extractor.EnsureInstalled` used
  go-ytdlp's `MustInstall`, which panics when the download fails (network
  down, empty cache) and dumped a full stack trace instead of a clean
  failure. Failed installs are now plain errors; the pre-run auto-install
  stays best-effort, and a missing tool still fails with the normal
  "yt-dlp is not available" message.
- **Capability/doctor now find go-ytdlp's versioned cache binaries**: the
  tool probe only looked for a bare `yt-dlp` on `PATH`, but go-ytdlp caches
  and resolves `yt-dlp-<version>` (e.g. `yt-dlp-2026.08.19`) inside the
  user cache dir. Resolution now falls back to that cache — bare name first,
  then the newest versioned file — so `doctor` and `status` report the same
  tools the engine actually uses.

## [0.8.0] - 2026-10-08

### Changed

- **Minimum Go version is now 1.27** (`go.mod` `go 1.27.2`), required by the
  upgraded `github.com/lrstanley/go-ytdlp v1.5.4`. Consumers must build with
  Go 1.27 or newer.
- Dependency refresh: `chromedp` v0.20.1 (and `cdproto` v0.157.9), `pgx/v5`
  v5.11.0, `go-ytdlp` v1.5.4, `klauspost/compress` v1.20.1, and current
  `golang.org/x/{crypto,sync,sys,term,text,time}`. The headless-Chrome paths
  were migrated to chromedp's generic action API (`Action[T]`, typed selectors,
  `Events` iterators); behavior is unchanged.

## [0.7.0] - 2026-10-08

### Added
- **Public reusable engine facade** (`github.com/sk3y04/provenance-engine/engine`): a stable, importable API for server-side consumers with `Engine.New`, `Engine.Resolve`, and `Engine.Download`. It wraps the existing `internal/*` implementations without copying extractors, accepts a `context.Context` on every call, reports presentation-neutral structured events through an `EventSink`, returns typed results and categorized `*engine.Error` failures, and never requires a CLI or terminal. The public CLI routes plain `grab` downloads through the same facade (`cmd/provenance/engine_adapter.go`). Includes package documentation (`docs/ENGINE.md`, package doc comment), compile-time external-consumer examples, and a standalone external module (`engine/externaltest`) verified in CI. Release process and licensing review items are documented in `docs/RELEASING.md`.
- **Structured engine events and typed errors**: new `internal/event` (structured `stage`/`progress`/`warning`/`item_done`/`retry`/`summary` events, a presentation-neutral `Sink`, and a bounded panic-recovering `Notifier`), `internal/engineerr` (categorized errors: validation, authentication_required, unsupported_source, rate_limited, temporary, canceled, external_tool, permanent), and `internal/render` (CLI event renderer). The yt-dlp single-URL Download/Resolve path now emits events and typed errors and writes nothing to the terminal when a sink is supplied; CLI/TUI behavior is unchanged while no sink is set.
- **Twitter/X hashtag media search**: `provenance grab --cookies cookies.txt 'x:#golang'` (also `'#golang'` and `https://x.com/hashtag/golang`) now downloads native X media attached to posts from the authenticated **Latest** hashtag search, restricted to posts with native media (`filter:media`). Uses the current web-client `SearchTimeline` GraphQL operation via POST, follows the bottom cursor until exhausted/`--limit`/cancellation/loop, and downloads photos, videos, and animated GIFs. Works through `collect add`/`sync` as a stable canonical `x:#tag` source with post-ID dedup. Output lands under `twitter/hashtags/<slug>/{images,videos,posts}`. Query ID is discovered from X web-client JS (env override `TWITTER_QUERY_SEARCH_TIMELINE`) and refreshed once on stale-query responses. Includes fixture-driven tests (no live X calls).
- **TUI Archive views**: new "Archive" main-menu entry with sub-views for every archive command — `archive url`, `archive session`, `archive import` (output directory), `import-pdf`, `import-git` (repo + ref), `import-docs` (site, scope, max pages), `import-openapi` (spec path), and `import-web` (URL, scope, max pages, screenshot, Chrome path) — each with its own input form, plus a "Vault init" and "Install yt-dlp" menu entry. Backed by `archive.IngestFromOutput`, which archives an output directory's captured manifests into the vault and returns the revision ID and entity count.
- **TUI Vault revision diff**: the Vault view now lists per-collection revisions; selecting two revisions (A then B) renders a field-level entity diff (added/removed/changed) in-TUI. New `RevisionStore.ListRevisionIDsByCollection` and `DeleteRevisionsByCollection` (FK-ordered cascade delete: relations → documents → entities → artifacts → revisions) in `internal/catalog`.
- **TUI Encode view**: "Encode videos" main-menu entry with dir/encoder/quality form driving the `encode` pipeline.
- **TUI config persistence** (`internal/tui/config.go`): last-used download form values, scan URL + advanced options, and encode settings are saved to a JSON store and re-applied to forms on next launch.
- **TUI session detail view**: `enter` in the Sessions list opens a detail view showing per-status counts and failed URLs with their last error; actions to export the session, export failed URLs, and resume the session (optionally retrying failed items). Main menu shows a banner for unfinished sessions with `R` to resume.
- **TUI archive search history**: last 20 search queries kept, navigable when returning to the search view.
- **TUI mouse support**: clicking a list row moves the cursor in list views and jumps form steps in forms.
- **Runner per-file throughput**: progress view now shows per-file speed (with decay so a stalled file doesn't hold a stale value).
- **Watch run status**: subscriptions now record `last_run_duration` and `last_run_status`; runs are marked `running` before download starts so an interrupted run reads as stuck rather than a stale success. `provenance watch run` records the same status/duration on finish.
- **Downloader media sniffing** (`internal/downloader/sniff.go`): `SniffExt` returns the canonical extension from magic bytes for png, jpg, gif, webp, mp4, webm, and bmp.

### Changed
- **Relicensed from GPL-3.0 to MIT**: the project is now distributed under the MIT license (`LICENSE`) so the private product can embed the engine without copyleft obligations. Redistribution must retain the copyright and license notice. This is a licensing change, not a functional one.
- **Repository/module rename (breaking import path)**: the Go module path is now `github.com/sk3y04/provenance-engine` (was `github.com/sk3y04/provenance`) and the GitHub repository is renamed to `provenance-engine`. The CLI binary and command remain `provenance`; no command, flag, exit-code, persistence, or output changes. External importers must update their import paths. See `docs/MIGRATION.md`.
- **Twitter/X animated GIFs**: `animated_gif` media now selects the highest-bitrate MP4 variant (as the downloader and `--include mp4` expect) instead of the still thumbnail; falls back to the still image only when no video variant is present.
- **TUI main menu**: expanded to 14 items (added Archive, Manifest, Encode videos); view enum grew from 12 to 25 views.
- **TUI filters**: session, watch, history, and collection filters now persist when leaving and re-entering a view (`/` restores the last accepted text).
- **Collection sync**: collection is reloaded before `RecordSync` to avoid a TOCTOU race with concurrent `AddSeen`/`RecordSync` calls.
- **Reddit media extensions**: API-reported extensions are validated against the accepted media set (lowercased; junk values like `"Image"` rejected), and downloaded files whose extension doesn't match their magic bytes are renamed to the real format.

### Fixed
- **Instagram/Twitter cookie headers from full browser exports**: `--cookies` files exported from a browser contain cookies for dozens of unrelated domains. The Instagram and Twitter extractors sent every cookie in the file, producing ~100KB `Cookie` headers that exceed the ~8KB HTTP/2 header-block limit enforced by Instagram's edge — every request died with `http2: server sent GOAWAY ... header-block-exceeds-max-size`. Cookies are now filtered to domains that apply to the requested hosts (plus an expiry check and per-name dedupe) before being sent.
- **Instagram REST API host cascade**: `i.instagram.com` rejects or rate-limits web sessions that `www.instagram.com` accepts (e.g. exports containing only `www.instagram.com` host cookies, or API-host challenges). All REST fetchers (profile feed, single post, stories, highlights) now fall back to `www.instagram.com/api/v1` when the first host rejects the session (401/403/404); rate limits are session-wide, so 429s do not trigger the fallback. A not-logged-in HTML response now prints a hint to re-export cookies including the `.instagram.com` domain.

## [2026-09-01]

### Added
- **Instagram Story Highlights**: `provenance grab https://www.instagram.com/stories/highlights/<id>/` now downloads every story in a highlight — images, videos, and multi-slide carousels — in one command. `ParseIgURL` recognizes the `/stories/highlights/<id>/` path as a new `highlight` target (kept distinct from active `/stories/<username>/` stories). `fetchIgHighlightStories` reuses the same `/feed/reels_media/` endpoint as active stories, addressing the reel via `reel_ids=highlight:<id>`, with `429`/rate-limit backoff, error-preview logging, and `igMaxAttempts` retry matching the story path. The owning username is resolved from the highlight response's `user`/`owner` object so output still lands under `instagram/<username>/`, falling back to `highlight_<id>` when unresolvable; a `supported_capabilities_new` POST recovery is included for highlights that return empty on the bare GET. Wired through `ScanInstagram`, `DownloadInstagram`, and `ScanInstagramResolved`.
- **AV1 transcode (`provenance encode`)**: batch-convert local video files to hardware-accelerated AV1 in an `.mkv` container, fanning work across one or more GPUs. New `internal/encode/` package (`encoder`, `runner`, `discover`, `run`) with `EncodeJob`, `Encoder`, and `Options`. Three hardware backends — Intel QuickSync (`av1_qsv`, `--encoder qsv`), AMD AMF (`av1_amf`, `amf`), NVIDIA NVENC (`av1_nvenc`, `nvenc`) — plus `auto`, which probes `ffmpeg -encoders` and selects the first available codec (QSV preferred); explicit selections are validated against the installed build. Quality uses a canonical QSV `global_quality` scale (1..51) translated per backend (AMF `cq_quality`, NVENC `crf` 1..33). Flags: `--dir`/`--file`, `--recursive`, `--ext` (default `mp4,mkv,mov,avi,ts,webm`), `--out`, `--suffix`, `--overwrite`, `--encoder`, `--devices` (render nodes/GPU indices, default `/dev/dri/renderD128`), `--quality` (30), `--preset` (per-backend mapped speed/efficiency hint), `--gop-seconds` (converted to a per-file frame interval via ffprobe-detected fps), `--lookahead-depth` (QSV max 100), `--bframes`, and `--dry-run` (prints the exact ffmpeg command without encoding). Inputs run through the shared `internal/worker` pool (one pool per device, permanent-error semantics), audio/subtitle streams and container metadata are copied, and source files are never modified. Encoder-mismatch errors carry the phrase `not supported by this ffmpeg build` so `diagnose` offers a hardware/hint recovery.

### Changed
- **Site routing**: refactored site classification and extractor internals; per-site host tables are now resolved at runtime instead of hardcoded.

## [0.6.1] - 2026-07-26

### Added
- **Instagram stories support**: `provenance grab https://www.instagram.com/stories/USERNAME/` now downloads current story media (images and videos) using the `/feed/reels_media/` API endpoint with `reel_ids` parameter.

### Changed
- **Reddit API base**: switched from `www.reddit.com` to `old.reddit.com` for the JSON API, which has a more permissive bot policy.
- **Reddit User-Agent**: changed from `provenance/1.0` to Chrome 131; added `Sec-Fetch-*`, `Accept-Language`, and `Referer` browser headers.
- **uTLS** (`internal/downloader/utls_transport.go`): updated Chrome fingerprint from `HelloChrome_120` to `HelloChrome_131`, added `NextProtos` ALPN negotiation and `ForceAttemptHTTP2`. Used only by the downloader when `BrowserTLS` is set (media downloads). Native extractor API clients (Instagram, Twitter) keep Go's standard TLS as uTLS causes EOF/handshake issues on some endpoints.

### Fixed
- **Instagram profile user ID resolution**: `web_profile_info` API endpoint no longer reliably returns user `pk`. Added multi-method cascade: primary API call with `Referer` header and fallback to `id` field, web page HTML scraping (`profilePage_` pattern, iOS deep link meta tags, `user_id` JSON), `?__a=1&__d=1` JSON endpoint, and `users/search` API endpoint as last resort.
- **`provenance collect add` command unregistered**: the `add` subcommand was defined but never attached to `collect` (missing `cmd.AddCommand(add)`), making `--limit` and other download flags unavailable when adding collections.
- **Cookies path stored as relative**: `buildOptions` now resolves `--cookies` paths to absolute via `filepath.Abs`, preventing "no such file" errors when syncing collections from a different working directory.

## [0.6.0] - 2026-07-26

### Added
- **TUI Collections view**: list all collections with Name, Last sync, New, Skip, URL table. Filter via `/`. `enter` for detail, `s` to sync, `S` to sync-all, `a` to archive.
- **TUI Collection detail view**: full metadata, seen count, last sync result. `s` sync, `a` archive actions.
- **TUI Vault view**: shows vault init status, archive collections with revision counts. Prompt to run `vault init` if not initialized.
- **`provenance --version`**: version flag on root cobra command.
- **Root CLI help text**: rewritten to describe the four progressive levels (grab/collect/archive/import), list all commands, reflect full product scope.
- **Main menu**: expanded from 7 to 10 items (Collections, Vault added). TUI view enum expanded from 9 to 12.
- `resolve.Error.Is()` method for `errors.Is` support.
- `NewTextContent` constructor in resolve package.
- `safeTruncate` for UTF-8 aware content truncation in git and docs importers.
- `collFilter` properly initialized in TUI model for nil safety.

### Fixed
- **Search SQL**: SELECT/Scan column mismatch corrected; `revision_id`/`collection_name` scan order fixed.
- **Artifacts table**: added `PRIMARY KEY (sha256)` to migration (was missing, causing `ON CONFLICT` SQL error).
- **Vault connectivity**: `ensureVaultStore()` auto-connects PG from `PROVENANCE_DATABASE_URL` for vault-dependent commands.
- **Revision ID determinism**: artifacts, entities, documents, relations sorted by stable key before SHA-256 ID computation.
- **Blobstore `List()`**: fixed doubled hash prefix in concatenation.
- **GC safety**: `isHex` now accepts uppercase `A-F` hex characters.
- **Body leak**: `docs.go` response body now closed immediately (defer-in-loop removed).
- **Retention performance**: `PruneRevisions` uses 1-pass load+sort instead of O(n log n) disk reads in sort comparator.
- **`GetRevision`**: now populates `Artifacts` from PostgreSQL query.
- **Blobstore race**: `O_EXCL` tmp collision on concurrent same-content `Put` handled gracefully.
- **Comment retries**: `fetchRdComments` now has 4-attempt retry with exponential backoff.
- **Diff safety**: `h[:12]` guarded against short hash strings to prevent panic.
- **Downloader cache**: `LastHash`/`LastPath` now populated for already-existing files.
- **Audio detection**: expanded from 3 to 9 audio extension formats.
- **Dedup fallback**: items without external IDs now use URL for deduplication.
- **Crosspost media**: `RdPostToItem` now iterates `CrosspostParentList`.
- **Instagram URLs**: canonical URL now uses correct prefix (`/p/`, `/reel/`, `/tv/`) based on post type.
- **Failure reporting**: partial download failures use actual session counts instead of marking all as failed.
- **Playlist detection**: uses yt-dlp extractor key instead of fragile URL substring.
- **Citation parse**: uses string splitting instead of `fmt.Sscanf`.
- **Vault TUI**: per-collection revision counts instead of global total.
- **Catalog race**: `UpsertCollection` TOCTOU fixed with `loadLocked`/`saveLocked` helpers.
- **Other**: regex compiled once in docs.go; `ListRunManifests` sorted; `ToolVersion` set in capture manifest; dead `ids` parameter removed.

### Changed
- CLI short description: "a universal media downloader" → "universal media collector, source archive, and knowledge vault"

## [0.5.2] - 2026-07-23

### Added
- **`archive/diff.go`**: `DiffRevisions(old, new) *DiffResult` — matches entities by `ExternalID`, reports added/removed/changed with field-level diffs.
- **`blobstore.List()`**: enumerates all stored blobs for GC.
- **`catalog/gc.go`**: `GarbageCollect(vaultRoot, dryRun)` — finds orphaned blobs by diffing filesystem against revision manifest references.
- **`catalog/retention.go`**: `PruneRevisions(vaultRoot, collectionName, keep)` — prunes old revisions keeping the last N.
- **CLI**: `provenance vault diff <idA> <idB>`, `vault gc --dry-run`, `vault retention prune --collection X --keep N`, `vault backup`.
- **CLI**: `provenance collect sync --every 24h` — repeating sync with `time.Ticker` loop.

## [0.5.1] - 2026-07-21

### Added
- **`internal/importers/web.go`**: chromedp-based web page archiver (`ImportWeb`) — navigates pages via headless Chrome, extracts rendered HTML, visible text, and page titles.
- **Multi-page crawl**: discovers same-scope links via `document.querySelectorAll`, bounded by `--max-pages`.
- **`ArtifactHTML`** constant in `archive/types.go` for HTML snapshot artifacts.
- **CLI**: `provenance archive import-web <URL>` with `--scope`, `--max-pages`, `--screenshot` flags.
- No Docker dependency — reuses existing `chromedp` infrastructure.

## [0.5.0] - 2026-07-18

### Added
- **`internal/importers/`**: technical knowledge importers for PDFs, Git repositories, static docs sites, and OpenAPI specs.
- **PDF importer**: extracts text per page via `ledongthuc/pdf`, stores original PDF as blob artifact, creates one `Document` per page with `RelContains` relations.
- **Git importer**: shallow clone via `git clone --depth 1`, resolves tag to commit SHA, walks `.md`/`.adoc`/`.txt`/README/LICENSE/CHANGELOG files as Documents.
- **Docs site importer**: sitemap discovery + link crawl, bounded by `--scope`/`--max-pages`, extracts headings and text.
- **OpenAPI importer**: parses YAML spec, generates `Document` per endpoint, creates `Entity` with `Kind: "api_spec"`.
- **CLI**: `archive import-pdf`, `import-git`, `import-docs`, `import-openapi` with `--ref`, `--scope`, `--max-pages` flags.

### Changed
- **Dependencies**: added `github.com/ledongthuc/pdf`, `github.com/yuin/goldmark`, `gopkg.in/yaml.v3`.

## [0.4.2] - 2026-07-16

### Added
- **`--include-comments`** and **`--max-comments`** flags: opt-in comment fetching with configurable limit (default 100).
- **Reddit comment fetching**: `fetchRdComments()` + `walkRdComments()` call `{permalink}.json`, recursively walk comment tree with depth bounding.
- **`CaptureItem.Text` population**: `recordCapture()` now reads post `.md` files and populates `CaptureItem.Text`, enabling full-text search of social post content in the archive.

## [0.4.1] - 2026-07-12

### Added
- **PostgreSQL integration**: `CatalogStore` interface; `PgStore` implementation using `pgx/v5` (connection pooling, transactional inserts).
- **Full-text search**: `plainto_tsquery`/`ts_rank`/`ts_headline` across entities and documents with GIN indexes and auto-update `tsvector` triggers.
- **SQL migration**: embedded schema creating `archive_collections`, `revisions`, `entities`, `documents`, `artifacts`, `relations` tables.
- **Dual-write archive**: `archive.IngestCaptureManifest` writes to both filesystem (blobs) and PostgreSQL (metadata) when store is available.
- **CLI**: `provenance vault init`, `vault show`, `vault cite` with `--entity`/`--format` flags, `provenance search <query>` with `--collection`/`--kind` flags.
- **Citation formatters**: `Markdown()`, `Plain()` (title, URL, date, author, SHA-256), `ToJSON()`, `FromEntity()` constructor.
- **TUI**: `viewArchiveSearch` — text input with search results, cursor navigation, ranked hits with headlines.

## [0.4.0] - 2026-07-08

### Added
- **`internal/blobstore/`**: SHA-256 content-addressed filesystem storage with `Put`/`Get`/`Exists`/`Remove`. Deduplication via hash collision. Atomic writes via `.tmp` → rename.
- **`internal/archive/`**: immutable vault domain model — `ArchiveCollection`, `Source`, `Revision`, `Entity`, `Artifact`, `Document`, `Relation`.
- **`IngestCaptureManifest`**: consumes capture manifests, verifies SHA-256, copies files to blob store, builds revision records.
- **`internal/catalog/`**: JSON persistence for archive collections.
- **`internal/citation/`**: stable citation references `provenance://collection@revision#entity`.
- **`provenance archive`**: CLI command tree — `archive url`, `archive collection`, `archive session`, `archive import`.
- Blobstore tests: Put/Get/Exists, deduplication, Remove.

## [0.3.2] - 2026-07-05

### Added
- **SHA-256 hashing in downloader**: `Download()` computes hash inline via `io.MultiWriter` with `sha256.New()`; stored in `Client.LastHash` and `Client.LastPath` on success.
- **Capture manifests**: `CaptureManifest`, `CaptureItem`, `TextCapture`, `CaptureOptions`, `VerificationResult` types in `internal/manifest/capture.go`.
- **`.provenance/` filesystem**: write/read/verify functions — `WriteCaptureManifest`, `WriteCaptureItem`, `VerifyCaptureDir`, `FileSha256`, `ListRunManifests`.
- **`collect sync --record`**: writes capture manifests to `<outputDir>/.provenance/`.
- **`provenance manifest show/verify`**: display and verify capture manifests.

## [0.3.1] - 2026-06-28

### Added
- **`internal/collection/`**: named, repeatable sync sources with seen-item tracking and incremental dedup.
- **CLI**: `provenance collect {add,list,show,sync,remove}` with all grab flags, `--dry-run`, `--all`.
- Collections persisted as JSON at `~/.cache/provenance/collections.json`.
- Resume support: each sync creates a resumable session (`collect-<name>-<timestamp>`).

### Changed
- **Terminal summary**: every `grab` prints structured counts (discovered/downloaded/skipped/failed/output) via `CountsReporter` with atomic counters.
- **TUI labels**: `"New download"` → `"New grab"` in main menu, form header, and runner title.
- **Runtime messages**: `"provenance download --batch"` → `"provenance grab --batch"`; `"video(s)"` → `"item(s)"`.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-06-20

### Changed
- **CLI**: Renamed `download` command to `grab`; `download` kept as hidden deprecated alias.
- **Module**: Path changed from `github.com/skey/provenance` to `github.com/sk3y04/provenance`.
- **Lint**: Migrated `.golangci.yml` to golangci-lint v2 format; added gosec exclusions.

### Added
- **`internal/resolve/`** package: shared result types (`Source`, `Item`, `MediaAsset`, `TextContent`) that all extractors normalise into.
- **`internal/resolve/errors.go`**: standardised error categories (`auth`, `rate_limit`, `unavailable`, `unsupported_url`, `resolve_failure`, `transfer_failure`).
- **Per-extractor adapters**: `YtdlpInfoToSource`, `TwTweetToItem`, `RdPostToItem`, `IgPostToItem` with canonical URLs, consistent `MediaKind`, `PublishedAt`, raw metadata.
